upports identification from factual-arm at-risk histories; its efficiency-bound and multiply robust estimation results inform the open semiparametric inference question.",
  "technical_internal_limitation": "The primitive counts are raw, nonnegative-integer-valued, and not globally bounded by \\(H\\). The condition \\(B+W\\le H\\) constrains one switched counterfactual branch after separately capping its prefix burden and residual increment; it is a substantive shape restriction, not a loss normalization and not a consequence of the response-tree universe. A finite-reserve mechanism gives a concrete compatible class, but no such mechanism has been established for SPRINT. Dahl's feasibility criterion can reject a proposed sensitivity cap statistically, but it cannot establish clinical credibility. The response-tree theorem preserves only the original arm-specific sequential censoring law on factual at-risk histories; independence between censoring and the entire cross-world response tree is neither assumed nor produced. Assigning independent errors to all branches would strengthen FFRCISTG to an NPSEM model and would not establish the stated claim.",
